#########################################################################
Date: Apr 2, 2025 16:19 PM

Subject: the 64 KB bufferfills in ~7.9 s of zero-read, and the observed D-Bus storm lasts ~29 s, causing
io_send: EAGAIN drops that appear as audio distortion.aise the pipe buffer to 512 KB with F_SETPIPE_SZ, giving a 62-s fill time at
the 8.1 KB/s ADPCM data rate and comfortably absorbing the worst-case scan storm.

Source: Sky
Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Damiano Barone <damiano.barone@sky.uk>
#########################################################################

--- bluez-5.48.orig/src/gatt-client.c
+++ bluez-5.48/src/gatt-client.c
@@ -1136,6 +1136,12 @@
 
 	if (pipe2(pipefd, O_DIRECT | O_NONBLOCK | O_CLOEXEC) < 0)
 		return btd_error_failed(msg, strerror(errno));
+	/* LLAMA-18285: increase notify pipe buffer from the 64 KB kernel default
+	 * to 512 KB so that brief ctrlm event-loop stalls (caused by D-Bus
+	 * congestion during LE scan storms) do not fill the pipe and produce
+	 * io_send: EAGAIN audio frame drops on the voice remote stream. */
+	if (fcntl(pipefd[1], F_SETPIPE_SZ, 512 * 1024) < 0)
+		DBG("Failed to increase GATT notify pipe buffer: %s", strerror(errno));
 
 	dir = dbus_message_has_member(msg, "AcquireWrite");
 
